			{
				"type": "Comment",
				"start": 0,
				"end": 463,
				"data": "\n\tAn authored blank line INSIDE a content text is not a run boundary — a run is a partition of\n\tnodes — so the fill collapses it and the layout is decided as if it were a space, for every\n\tcontainer kind alike. A blank BESIDE a sibling does bound the run and is preserved (the edge\n\tcontrol), and authored boundary air still holds the multiline form — a blank spelling of\n\tthat air included, which collapses to the one break it asks for (the air control).\n"
			},
